There are two ways in which this can be run.
1) By using the same operator each time
2) By creating a new operator each time


Algorithm 1
- Read old username 
- Generate new flag
- Connect to port 7413 
- Send old username, followed by space, followed by new flag
- The operator will answer "Last time we were talking about "..." 
  where "..." is the old flag
- Optional: send some random
- Send "exit"
Next time the newly set flag will be returned.

Algorithm 2
- Read old username 
- Generate new username and new flag
- Connect to port 7413 
- Send old username, followed by space, followed by a random string
- The operator will answer "Last time we were talking about "..." 
  where "..." is the old flag
- Send "exit"
- Connect to port 7413 (again) 
- Send new username, followed by space, followed by new flag
- new username will be the "old username" next time
 

